findings.recommendation:
In AuthService.applyRegistration(), explicitly reset every authority/role-bearing field on the repurposed slot. Minimum patch:

```java
user.setDeletedAt(null);
user.setSuperAdmin(false);              // ADD
user.setPasswordResetTokenHash(null);
user.setPasswordResetExpiresAt(null);
user.setPasswordResetUsedAt(null);
```

Longer-term, treat repurposing as a hard reset: instantiate a new User and copy only id+createdAt from the existing document, so any future authority field added to the schema is excluded by default. Add a unit test that registers against a soft-deleted superadmin and asserts isSuperAdmin == false on the resulting document.
